# EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR: Undefined variable: 'no_such_variable'
#~
A read of a variable that was never declared must be rejected with the
undefined-variable diagnostic.

This used to read `y := no_such_variable + 1;` and passed on the wrong error:
inside a method an unknown name on the left of an operator is taken as a new
type-inferred local, so obc reported "Invalid operation '+' between types: Var
and Int" and never said the variable was undefined. The string-interpolation
reader resolves the name against the declared symbols and names it.
~#
class BadUndefinedVar {
    function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
        "{$no_such_variable}"->PrintLine();
    }
}
